  "metadata": {
    "title": "Getting Started",
    "description": "Install @capgo/capacitor-persistent-uuid and create a stable app UUID.",
    "sidebar": {
      "order": 2
    }
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 2,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 2,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Install"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 4,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 4,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "You can use our AI-Assisted Setup to install the plugin. Add the Capgo skills to your AI tool using the following command:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 6,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "bash",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "npx skills add https://github.com/Cap-go/capgo-skills --skill capacitor-plugins"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 10,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 10,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Then use the following prompt:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 12,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "text",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "Use the `capacitor-plugins` skill from `Cap-go/capgo-skills` to install the `@capgo/capacitor-persistent-uuid` plugin in my project."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 16,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 16,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "If you prefer Manual Setup, install the plugin by running the following commands and follow the platform-specific instructions below:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 18,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "bash",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "bun add @capgo/capacitor-persistent-uuid\nbunx cap sync"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 23,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 23,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Import"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 25,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "typescript",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "import { PersistentUuid } from '@capgo/capacitor-persistent-uuid';"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 29,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 29,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Read Or Create The UUID"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 31,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "typescript",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "import { PersistentUuid } from '@capgo/capacitor-persistent-uuid';\n\nconst result = await PersistentUuid.getId();\n\nconsole.log(result.id);\nconsole.log(result.scope);\nconsole.log(result.created);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 41,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 41,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "The first call creates and stores a UUID. Later calls return the same UUID for the same scope."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 43,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 43,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Use A Stable Custom Scope"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 45,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 45,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "The native default scope is the package name on Android and the bundle identifier on iOS. If debug and production builds use different package identifiers but should share one UUID, pass a shared scope."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 47,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "typescript",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "const result = await PersistentUuid.getId({\n  scope: 'com.example.app',\n});"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 53,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 53,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Reset The UUID"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 55,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 55,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Call resetId when the user logs out, requests a privacy reset, or when automated tests need a new identifier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "location": {
        "line": 57,
        "column": 1
      },
      "lang": "typescript",
      "meta": null,
      "text": "const replacement = await PersistentUuid.resetId();\nconsole.log(replacement.id);"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "location": {
        "line": 62,
        "column": 1
      },
      "depth": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 62,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "Persistence Expectations"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "location": {
        "line": 64,
        "column": 1
      },
      "ordered": false,
      "start": null,
      "spread": false,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 64,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 64,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 64,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "Android can survive uninstall and reinstall, including Android Studio and Play installs with different signing keys, when the package name or custom scope is stable."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 65,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 65,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 65,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "iOS survives app updates and iOS updates while Keychain access rules remain the same."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listItem",
          "location": {
            "line": 66,
            "column": 1
          },
          "spread": false,
          "checked": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "location": {
                "line": 66,
                "column": 3
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 66,
                    "column": 3
                  },
                  "text": "Web uses localStorage and is only a development fallback."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
